{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1800","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E2. Unforgivable Curse (hard version)"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This is a complex version of the problem. This version has no additional restrictions on the number $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The chief wizard of the Wizengamot once caught the evil wizard Drahyrt, but the evil wizard has returned and wants revenge on the chief wizard. So he stole "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ from his student Harry."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" — is a $$$n$$$-length string of lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Drahyrt wants to replace "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with an unforgivable curse — string $$$t$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Dragirt, using ancient magic, can swap letters at a distance $$$k$$$ or $$$k+1$$$ in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" as many times as he wants. In other words, Drahyrt can change letters in positions $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ if $$$|i-j|=k$$$ or $$$|i-j|=k+1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, if $$$k = 3, s = $$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"talant"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and $$$t = $$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"atltna"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", Drahyrt can act as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" swap the letters at positions $$$1$$$ and $$$4$$$ to get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aaltnt"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" swap the letters at positions $$$2$$$ and $$$6$$$ to get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"atltna"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spells"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ and $$$t$$$. Can Drahyrt change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ to $$$t$$$?"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input gives a single integer $$$T$$$ ($$$1 \\le T \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases in the test."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Descriptions of the test cases are follow."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n, k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spells"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the number $$$k$$$ such that Drahyrt can change letters in a spell at a distance $$$k$$$ or $$$k+1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line gives "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ — a string of length $$$n$$$ consisting of lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The third line gives "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$t$$$ — a string of length $$$n$$$ consisting of lowercase Latin letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ values over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$. Note that there is no limit on the sum of $$$k$$$ values over all test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a separate line \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if Drahyrt can change "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"spell"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$s$$$ to $$$t$$$ and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (for example, lines \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as positive answer)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n6 3\ntalant\natltna\n7 1\nabacaba\naaaabbc\n12 6\nabracadabraa\navadakedavra\n5 3\naccio\ncicao\n5 4\nlumos\nmolus\n4 3\nuwjt\ntwju\n4 3\nkvpx\nvxpk\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first case is explained in the condition."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second case, we can swap adjacent letters, so we can sort the string using bubble sorting, for example."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third case, we can show that from the string $$$s$$$ we cannot get the string $$$t$$$ by swapping letters at a distance of $$$6$$$ or $$$7$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth case, for example, the following sequence of transformations is appropriate:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"accio"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aocic"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cocia"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"iocca"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aocci"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"aicco"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" $$$\\rightarrow$$$ \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"cicao"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fifth case, we can show that it is impossible to get the string $$$s$$$ from the string $$$t$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the sixth example, it is enough to swap the two outermost letters."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E2","problemCode":"1800E2","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1800/problem/E2"}